From db570b7c20855a0dab609f2365d6a5243f1e7dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] feat(deployment): add a tgi-process launcher

Services whose runtime provider is tgi could be scheduled but never
deployed, because only the fake and vLLM launchers existed.
TGIProcessLauncher runs text-generation-launcher on the control plane
host on top of the shared process launcher, so it gets the same
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES handling, /health readiness wait and session-wide
stop as vllm-process, and serves the tgi-generate protocol the gateway
already routes to /generate_stream.

TGI's defaults make two instances on one host collide: the router talks
to its shards over /tmp/text-generation-server-<rank> and the shards
rendezvous on port 29500. Each instance therefore gets a second free
port as --master-port and a private 0700 temporary directory for
--shard-uds-path. The launcher removes the directory once the instance
is stopped, has exited and is launched again, or could not be started
at all.

FORGEMESH_RUNTIME_LAUNCHER=tgi-process is configured through
FORGEMESH_TGI_COMMAND, FORGEMESH_TGI_BIND_HOST,
FORGEMESH_TGI_ADVERTISE_HOST, FORGEMESH_TGI_READY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS and
FORGEMESH_TGI_STOP_GRACE_SECONDS, with the same defaults and inventory
rules as the vLLM variables. Without FORGEMESH_TGI_COMMAND the default
text-generation-launcher must be on PATH, so a host without TGI refuses
to start instead of failing every deployment later.
